# Git and pull request policy

Policy version: 1

Only `git-good` may perform mutating Git or pull request operations. Parent agents and all other agents are read-only and may use only `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`, and `git show`.

Route every mutation through `.cursor/agents/git-good.md`, which must follow the canonical private skill at `/agent/repos/docfoundry-skills/.cursor/skills/git-good/SKILL.md`.

- Create feature work from `dev` and merge it into `dev`.
- Test features before integration, then test the integrated candidate on `dev`.
- Promote releases from `dev` to `main`.
- Deploy production only from `main`.
- Use a hotfix only with explicit authorization, target `main`, and sync the merged hotfix back to `dev`.
- Never merge without an explicit user instruction to merge.

One-time bootstrap exception: the parent agent may create the installation commit that introduces `git-good`. After that commit, only `git-good` may mutate Git or pull requests.
